==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|synæresis||dated}}
* {{alter|en|synairesis||uncommon}}
* {{alter|en|syneresis||US}}

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|grc|συναίρεσις||unification}}, from {{m|grc|συν-||together}} + {{m|grc|αἵρεσις||taking}}, from {{m|grc|αἱρέω||I take}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/sɪnˈɛɹəsɪs/}}

===Noun===
{{examples|sense=linguistics, prosody|examples=contraction of the ''-ew'' ({{IPAchar|/uː/|lang=en}}) and ''or-'' ({{IPAchar|/oʊɹ/|lang=en}}) of ''[[New Orleans]]'' into {{IPAchar|/'''nɔː'''lənz/|lang=en}}.}}
{{en-noun|~|synaereses}}

# {{lb|en|linguistics|prosody}} The [[contraction]] of two [[vowel]]s into a [[diphthong]] or a [[long vowel]].
#: {{hyper|en|metaplasm}}
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} The [[separating]] out of the [[liquid]] from a [[gel]].

